course: dictionary
lesson: 9413
title: Squeak: a sound and a way of getting by
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A squeak is a short, high, thin sound, like a mouse or a door that needs oil. «Chloe's guinea pigs squeak like a car alarm every morning.» The clue is the car alarm: it is loud and high, so a squeak is a high sound, even if it is small.
explain: Squeak can also be a verb, something you do: «The slide squeaks when the legs grip the metal.» Ask yourself: what is happening? If something is making a thin, high noise, squeak means that noise.
explain: The phrase «squeak through» or «squeak by» is different. It means you only just pass or win. «I squeaked through the spelling test!» means you passed, but only just. Here the word is about how close you were, not about sound.
fact: A squeak is a short, high, thin sound.
fact: To squeak means to make that sound.
fact: «Squeak through» or «squeak by» means to only just pass or win.
fact: «Not a squeak» means no sound at all, not even a tiny one.
fact: In science, squeaks are high-pitched sounds made by fast vibrations.
exercise: «Chloe's guinea pigs squeak like a car alarm every morning.» What does squeak mean here? | A heavy bump | *A short, high sound | A bright flash of light | A slow, deep groan
exercise: «On holiday the neighbour feeds them, and they don't squeak once.» In this sentence, what does squeak mean? | *To make a short, high sound | To run very fast | To feed someone | To pass a test
exercise: Sam got 5 out of 10 and said, «I only just squeaked through!» What does squeaked through mean? | Lost his voice | *Only just passed | Won by a huge margin | Failed very badly
test: «A slide is faster on a smooth mat, because bare, sweaty legs grip a metal slide, squeak and slow you down.» What does squeak mean in this sentence? | Go up very high | *Make a high, thin sound | Shine brightly | Stop completely
test: Mum says, «The squeaky wheel gets the grease.» What does this saying mean? | Only toys can be squeaky | *The person who complains loudly gets noticed and helped | Quiet people always win | Wheels must be cleaned to go fast
exam: The mouse gave a tiny ___ when the cat came into the room. | *squeak | Stripe | Whisper | Tiny
